        <mxCell id="rel-order-payment-label" value="payment_id FK" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#fff3e0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=1;fontSize=8" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1390" y="435" width="80" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="rel-mongo-kafka" value="CDC" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;dashed=1;endArrow=classic;endFill=1;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1" edge="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="300" y="480" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="300" y="850" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rel-mongo-kafka-label" value="oplog → Kafka&#xa;product.changes" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#e1bee7;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=1;fontSize=8" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="230" y="650" width="80" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="rel-kafka-es" value="ES Indexer" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;dashed=1;endArrow=classic;endFill=1;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1" edge="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="400" y="850" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="400" y="820" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- ========== KEY PATTERNS ========== -->
        
        <mxCell id="patterns-box" value="🔑 KEY DATA PATTERNS" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e3f2fd;strokeColor=#1976d2;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1230" width="2340" height="230" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="patterns-text" value="1. **reserved_qty Pattern (Inventory)**: available = qty - reserved_qty. During checkout: increment reserved_qty (stock removed from pool but NOT deducted). After payment webhook: decrement both qty and reserved_qty atomically. Prevents overselling without permanently locking stock.&#xa;&#xa;2. **Idempotency via UNIQUE Constraint (Payments)**: UNIQUE(order_id) on payments table. Webhook handler: SELECT before INSERT. If row exists → 200 OK (already processed, safe to replay). If not → BEGIN; INSERT; UPDATE orders; UPDATE inventory; COMMIT. Prevents double-charge on webhook retry.&#xa;&#xa;3. **ON CONFLICT Upsert (Cart)**: Composite PRIMARY KEY (cart_id, product_id). INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET qty = qty + EXCLUDED.qty. Handles race: user adds same product from mobile + web simultaneously. One row per product guaranteed.&#xa;&#xa;4. **CDC for Search Sync (MongoDB → Elasticsearch)**: Product Service writes only to MongoDB. MongoDB oplog → Kafka topic → ES indexer consumer. Decoupled, eventual consistency (1-2 sec lag acceptable for search). ES down? Kafka offset replay rebuilds index.&#xa;&#xa;5. **Cache-Aside Pattern (Redis)**: Read from cache first. If miss → fetch from DB → SET with TTL. On update → DEL cache key (invalidation). Write-through NOT used (inventory changes frequently, cache would thrash).&#xa;&#xa;6. **Distributed Lock Auto-Expiry (Redis SETNX)**: SETNX lock:inventory:{pid} {session} EX 30. If service crashes mid-checkout, lock expires after 30 sec. Next user can proceed. No manual cleanup, no deadlock risk.&#xa;&#xa;7. **Event-Driven Decoupling (Kafka)**: Payment Service publishes payment.success event, returns 200 immediately. Notification, Warehouse, Analytics consume independently. One slow/failed consumer doesn't block checkout. Retry from Kafka offset.&#xa;&#xa;8. **Flexible Schema (MongoDB)**: Products stored as documents with category-specific fields in 'specifications' object. Mobile: {RAM, storage}. Books: {author, ISBN}. No ALTER TABLE for new categories. Elasticsearch extracts common fields (brand, color) for faceted search.&#xa;&#xa;9. **Partitioned Orders (MySQL)**: PARTITION BY RANGE (YEAR*100 + MONTH). Historical queries (user's past 6 months) scan fewer partitions. Archival: old partitions moved to cold storage (S3). Query performance stays constant as data grows.&#xa;&#xa;10. **At-Least-Once Delivery (Kafka)**: Consumer commits offset AFTER processing. If consumer crashes mid-processing, event replayed. Handlers MUST be idempotent (webhook uses SELECT before INSERT, warehouse checks shipment_id before shipping)." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=9" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="1260" width="2320" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- ========== SCALE NUMBERS ========== -->
        
        <mxCell id="scale-box" value="📊 SCALE &amp; CAPACITY" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#e65100;strokeWidth=3;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1480" width="2340" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="scale-text" value="**MongoDB**: 100M products × 5KB = 500GB. Sharded by category (10 shards × 50GB each). 3-replica set per shard. Write: 1K products/sec (sellers uploading). Read: 10K reads/sec (product pages). Index size: 50GB (product_id, category+price).&#xa;&#xa;**PostgreSQL Inventory**: 100M products × 200 bytes = 20GB. Single primary (multi-AZ failover). Write: 100 checkouts/sec peak (reservations). Read: 1K inventory checks/sec. Connection pool: 200 conns (PgBouncer). SELECT FOR UPDATE contention mitigated by Redis distributed lock layer.&#xa;&#xa;**MySQL Orders**: 1M orders/day × 2KB = 2GB/day = 730GB/year. Partitioned monthly (12 partitions active, old partitions archived). Write: 100 orders/sec peak. Read: 5K order status checks/sec (user polling). Index: (user_id, created_at) for &quot;my orders&quot; queries.&#xa;&#xa;**Elasticsearch**: 100M products × 3KB indexed = 300GB. 10-node cluster (30GB per node). Queries: 100K search/sec peak (60% cached by Redis). Refresh interval: 1s (near real-time). CDC lag: 1-2 sec avg, 10 sec p99 (bulk import spikes).&#xa;&#xa;**Redis**: 50GB total. Cart: 10M users × 2KB = 20GB (HSET). Product cache: 10M hot products × 1KB = 10GB. Search cache: 10M queries × 1KB = 10GB. Locks: 1000 concurrent checkouts × 100 bytes = 100KB (negligible). Eviction: allkeys-lru. Persistence: RDB + AOF.&#xa;&#xa;**Kafka**: 6 topics × 12 partitions = 72 partitions. Throughput: 10K events/sec. Retention: 7 days (financial events 30 days). Storage: 10K events/sec × 1KB × 604800 sec = 6GB/week. Replication factor: 3 (durability). Consumer lag: &lt;1 sec p99." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=8" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="1510" width="2320" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
